 "chapter": {
  "number": 10,
  "introduction": null,
  "content": [
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 13,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "young -- little. Cf. Matthew 5:16"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 16,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "blessed them -- In Hebrew custom, a father's act. (Cf) Genesis 27:38\n\n\"He had no children that He might adopt all children.\"--Bengel."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 18,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "Why callest -- Par., Believing Me to be but a human teacher, why callest thou Me \"good,\" etc."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 24,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "astonished -- Or, amazed, i.e. as Jews: knowing that temporal prosperity was, to the Jew as such, a token of divine favour. e.g. Deuteronomy 28:1-12."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 25,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "eye of -- It has been thought the reference here was to a postern door set in a gate of Jerusalem."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 28,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "Then Peter -- Cf. See note 2, Matthew 19:27-30\n\n(See Scofield \"Matthew 19:28\")"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 33,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "Son of man -- (See Scofield \"Matthew 8:20\")"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 45,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "life -- Or, soul. Cf. Isaiah 53:10,12 (Greek - ἀπόλλυμι,\" the soul or the essential life, not as commonly, \"zoe,\" the active life)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 46,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "And they -- Cf. (See Scofield \"Matthew 20:30\")"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 51,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "Lord -- Gr. \"Rabboni,\" my Master, a term of reverent love. Cf. John 20:16."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
